• If yes: was anything altered — slimmed, enhanced, reshaped, or age-shifted?
• If yes: was any detail dropped?
• If universal was not mentioned: did Muse create the attire?
• If universal was not mentioned: did Muse create the likeness?
• If universal was not mentioned: did Muse create the body measurements, height, and age?
4. Never copy the reference's staging

• Were the reference image's gestures copied?
• Were the reference image's postures copied?
• Was the reference image's lighting copied?
• Were the reference image's sizes copied?
• Was the reference image's background copied?
• Was the reference image's composition copied?
• Is every gesture in this scene original to this scene?
• Is every posture in this scene original to this scene?
• Is every composition in this scene original to this scene?
5. Real people, no stand-ins

• Is the likeness accurate to real life as requested?
• Is there any generic stand-in?
• Are all accessories kept — including accessories not held in hand?
• Are the same bums, thighs, busts, hips, hair, attire, and details kept?
Final gate

• Run every question above against every tych.
• Every question passes, or the scene does not ship.
• When a question fails, fix the scene. Never weaken the question.

