Realism and Lighting Audits — Forced Audit Checklist

General scope. These audits apply to any scene. No scene specifics. No named individuals. Every question is sourced from the standing rules. Nothing here is invented.

The forcing rule

• The AI runs every question in this document against every tych before delivering output.
• Every question must pass. One failure means the scene fails.
• When a question fails, fix the scene. Never weaken the question.
• No skipping. No leniency. No redos counted as passes.
1. Documentary photography only

• Is the output authentic, in-color documentary photography?
• Is it unretouched?
• Is there natural skin texture?
• Is the lighting candid and natural?
• Is there any film grain?
• Is there any black-and-white filter?
2. Banned aesthetics — zero tolerance

• Is there any art, painting, or art style?
• Is there any digital render, CGI, or 3D model?
• Is there any airbrushing, digital smoothing, or digital simulation?
• Is there any staged lighting or golden hour?
• Is there anything artificial or synthetic?
• Is there any clinical render look?
3. Unified naked-eye realism

• Is there unified naked-eye realism?
• Is the realism tangible, solid, and weighted?
• Are the humans detailed biological humans — never blank, never lifeless?
• Does the image look like unfiltered amateur candid realism?
• Is it professional-looking?
• Is it staged-looking?
• Is it polished-looking?
4. One light direction

• Is there exactly one light direction?
• Are the shadows consistent?
• Do contact points carry true contact shadows?
• Is there ambient occlusion where bodies meet surfaces?
• Is there any detached shadow?
• Is there any missing contact shadow?
5. One camera, one projection

• Does the entire image exist within one continuous three-dimensional physical space?
• Was it photographed from one camera at one precise position, height, orientation, focal length, and perspective?
• Do humans and all surrounding objects share exactly the same camera geometry?
• Was the human generated with a separate virtual camera and placed into the environment?
• Was the human generated as an independent image and composited in?
• Do all corresponding lines, planes, depth relationships, and vanishing directions agree across the entire image?
• Does the human genuinely occupy the indicated three-dimensional location?
• One camera, one projection, one horizon, one depth system, one optical viewpoint. Is that true here?
6. No lens distortion

• Is there any fisheye distortion?
• Is there any wide-angle or ultra-wide distortion?
• Is there any tilt-shift or miniature look?
• Is there any barrel distortion or peripheral lens stretching?
• Is there any forced perspective?
• Is there any trick angle or lens gimmick faking size, distance, or scale?
• Is the camera a normal lens at the 25-30 degree field-of-view baseline?
7. No perspective warping of body parts

• Does the camera make any body part look bigger than its true size?
• Does the camera make any body part look smaller, stretched, or warped?
• Does any hand reach toward the camera?
• Does any arm extend toward the lens?
• Does any foot, knee, or elbow jut toward the camera?
• Does any body part sit much closer to the lens than the rest of the body?
• Is foreshortening used only where it enlarges, shrinks, or distorts nothing?
8. Camera unacknowledged

• Does anyone look into the lens?
• Does anyone pose for the camera?
• Does anyone present anything to the camera?
• Does anyone hold anything out toward the viewer?
• Does anyone turn toward the camera?
• Does anyone orient their body toward the camera?
• Is every action directed at the scene, with nothing directed at the viewer?
• Are there any first-person hands in frame?
• Is any gaze conveyed through anything other than the selected camera angles?
9. No camera cheats for size

• Did the camera pan out or zoom out to show size differences?
• Did the camera enlarge the human for detail?
• Did the camera change the human's stated size in any way?
• Does the camera record honestly, manufacturing nothing the physical scene does not have?
Final gate

• Run every question above against every tych.
• Every question passes, or the scene does not ship.
• When a question fails, fix the scene. Never weaken the question.

